      "title": "Graduate Assistant GRIP Supervisor",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant GRIP Supervisor Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Graduate Assistant GRIP Supervisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Concord University is a small public, comprehensive institution with an enrollment of around 1800 students. The University is located in a scenic, small-town setting in the mountains of southern West Virginia with access to year-round outdoor recreation activities. While life is slower in the Appalachians, Athens is within driving distance to metropolitan areas in West Virginia, Virginia, North Carolina, and Washington, DC. Concord has a strong commitment to the principle of diversity and in that spirit seeks a broad representation of candidates including women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Graduate Assistant Position Title Graduate Assistant GRIP Supervisor Working Title Scheduled Hours Per Week 25 FLSA Status Non-Exempt Job Summary Job Summary Athletic GRIP (Athletic Retention Graduation Program) supervisor -Oversee athletic study hall -Communicate and schedule athletic GRIP mentors/ tutors. -Work closely with Head Coaches to provide student-athletes with academic support. -Input midterm grades and oversee student-athlete study hall hours. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility -Oversee athletic study hall. % of Time Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification Bachelors degree required Required Skills Required Experience Type of experience Needed Oversee Study Hall Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) None, up to 6 months Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Concord University is a small public, comprehensive institution with an enrollment of around 1800 students. The University is located in a scenic, small-town setting in the mountains of southern West Virginia with access to year-round outdoor recreation activities. While life is slower in the Appalachians, Athens is within driving distance to metropolitan areas in West Virginia, Virginia, North Carolina, and Washington, DC. Concord has a strong commitment to the principle of diversity and in that spirit seeks a broad representation of candidates including women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/2210 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other 