    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3407": {
      "title": "Chief Human Resources Officer",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Chief Human Resources Officer Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Chief Human Resources Officer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Category Staff Position Title Chief Human Resources Officer Working Title Scheduled Hours Per Week 37.5 FLSA Status Exempt Job Summary Job Summary Concord University seeks a collaborative, experienced, and student-centered leader to serve as the Chief Human Resources Officer. Reporting to the President and serving on Cabinet, the Chief Human Resources Officer provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for all human resources functions, including recruitment and retention, employee relations, disciplinary action, up to and including termination, compensation and classification, benefits administration, performance management, compliance, professional development, and policy administration. The Chief Human Resources Officer serves as a trusted advisor to university leadership and works closely with faculty, staff, and administrators to foster a positive workplace culture that supports employee success and advances the University’s mission. The successful candidate will bring a strong understanding of higher education human resources, a commitment to customer service, and the ability to balance strategic planning with day-to-day operational responsibilities. This position will play a key leadership role in strengthening employee engagement, supporting workplace culture initiatives, and helping the University continue to be an employer of choice. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Human Resources Leadership Provide leadership and oversight for all human resources functions and operations. Develop and implement HR strategies that support the University’s strategic priorities and workforce needs. Serve as a resource to university leadership on employment-related matters, organizational effectiveness, and employee engagement. Foster a workplace culture that promotes professionalism, collaboration, inclusion, and employee well-being Partner with university leadership to identify opportunities to enhance employee satisfaction, workplace effectiveness, and organizational culture. Serve on the President’s Cabinet and report directly to the President. Supervise human resources staff and risk management staff. Responsible for ensuring deadlines are met for all required human resources and employment reporting to HEPC , the Legislature, the federal government, etc. are met. Serve on various national, statewide and university committees as necessary. Oversight of the HR functions for the Concord Research Development Corporation. Employee Engagement and Organizational Development Lead initiatives designed to improve employee engagement, morale, retention, and workplace satisfaction. Analyze employee survey data, including institutional climate and workplace satisfaction surveys, and develop recommendations for continuous improvement. Collaborate with campus leadership, faculty, and staff to implement strategies that support a positive and productive work environment. Support organizational development efforts, succession planning, leadership development, and workforce planning initiatives. Create and maintain the university organizational structure in conjunction with the President and governing board. Coordinate employee recognition and appreciation programs that reinforce the University’s values and mission. Talent Acquisition and Retention Lead recruitment and oversee the onboarding efforts for faculty, staff, and administrators. Develop strategies to attract, retain, and support a talented and diverse workforce. Monitor workforce trends and recommend improvements to hiring and retention practices. Managing the search, interview and hiring processes for senior university leadership and other executive roles, in conjunction with the President and consistent with state code and all applicable rules and policies. Employee Relations and Performance Management Provide guidance, support and oversight regarding employee relations matters, conflict resolution, and workplace concerns. Administer performance evaluation processes and support employee development initiatives. Assist supervisors in addressing performance, disciplinary, and workplace issues in a fair and consistent manner. Compensation, Benefits, and Compliance Oversight of university compensation and classification programs and support salary studies and market analyses as necessary or as mandated by state code or HEPC rules and policies reporting for such requirements. Oversight of employee benefits administration and serve as a liaison with state agencies and benefit providers. Ensure compliance with federal and state employment laws, regulations, and university policies. Interfacing directly with legal counsel, risk management, etc., to handle external complaints and to mitigate risk. Working with Risk Management to handle EEOC , BOL , Civil Rights, Human Rights, etc. complaints as well as serve as a representative of the university in grievances. Prepare disciplinary notices, improvement plans, investigative reports, etc. Maintain HR policies and procedures and recommend revisions as needed. Training and Professional Development Coordinate employee training and professional development opportunities. Support leadership development and succession planning efforts. Promote programs that enhance employee engagement and workplace effectiveness. Human Resources Operations Maintain accurate personnel records and HR reporting systems. Utilize data and analytics to inform decision-making and improve HR services. Oversee HR processes and identify opportunities for increased efficiency and effectiveness. Reviewing all major university personnel policies, handbook revisions, and structural reorganization proposals before adoption. Responsible for leading, developing, and managing legally compliant employee programs and practices, including EEO . Manages, modifies, etc., all Board of Governor’s policies that relate to employment, HR, disciplinary action, compliance, etc. Handles all terminations and suspensions. Serve as lead on handling employee complaints. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, Public Administration, Organizational Leadership, or a related field. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible professional human resources experience at a high level. Demonstrated knowledge of employment laws, regulations, and human resources best practices. Strong interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills. Strong understanding of best practices for human resources professionals. Experience managing confidential and sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. Ability to work effectively with diverse constituencies and manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment. Preferred Qualifications Human resources experience within higher education. Experience working in a public institution or complex organizational environment as a Chief Human Resources Officer or Vice President for Human Resources, or similar high-level human resources professional. Professional certification such as SHRM -CP, SHRM - SCP , PHR , or SPHR . Experience leading employee engagement initiatives, workplace culture assessments, and organizational development efforts. Experience interpreting employee satisfaction survey results and implementing action plans based on findings. Knowledge of West Virginia higher education personnel policies and procedures HRIS systems and Microsoft Office. Extensive knowledge of Excel is a plus. % of Time Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Master's Required Licenses/Certification Required Skills Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong leadership and organizational skills. Ability to interpret and apply employment laws, regulations, and policies. Excellent judgment, problem-solving, and conflict-resolution abilities. Commitment to customer service and employee support. Ability to build trust and maintain effective working relationships across the institution. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to use data to drive decision-making and organizational improvement. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible professional human resources experience at a high level. Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3402 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3396": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Admissions Counselor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Concord University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a state Normal School to prepare teachers, Concord University (CU) is a public, career focused liberal arts institution located in rural southern West Virginia. Concord University (CU) offers talented individuals a wide array of fulfilling career opportunities from entry through academic or administrative professional levels. To maintain an outstanding talent pool, we employ individuals regionally, nationally, and internationally to attract top candidates. If you are looking for more than just a job, then I encourage you to browse our website and visit our job opportunities regularly. Learn more about Concord University and why it should be your first choice, not only for quality educational opportunities but also for exemplary employment. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply. This is a temporary, full-time position. Temporary positions are not eligible for Concord University employee benefits, except as may be required by applicable law. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Staff Position Title Admissions Counselor Working Title Admissions Counselor Scheduled Hours Per Week Salary FLSA Status Exempt Job Summary Job Summary The admissions counselor will recruit potential students and assist them and their families in the areas of admissions, financial aid, scholarships and registration. The candidate must have the ability to communicate effectively with people of diverse ethnic, socioeconomic, and educational backgrounds and a variety of interpersonal skills to interact appropriately in situations ranging from large meetings to individual appointments. This is a temporary appointment intended to support the Office of Admissions during a period of increased operational need. This position is not eligible for Concord University employee benefits, except as required by federal or state law. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility The individual will travel extensively both in-state and out-of-state for the purpose of general student recruitment. Represents the university at various off-campus events on weekends. Duties will involve the collection of contact and academic information, disbursal of recruitment material as well as answering questions and establishing a dialogue with potential students. Specifically information to be disbursed will include but not limited to admissions procedures, financial aid, scholarships, unique educational opportunity programs, campus events, and general information concerning degree programs. This position is also expected to provide such information and to establish professional relationships with key high school counselors and personnel. Reviews prospective students applications and directs them to the appropriate sources for guidance on courses of study, financial aid, scholarships, or other information. Meets with prospective students and answers questions about the university, areas of study, and opportunities for students. Assist in the planning and implementation of recruitment and other admissions activities and special projects % of Time 50 Duty/Responsibility Counselor will assist in the areas of but not limited to the evaluation of high school transcripts, GPA conversion, and the maintenance of communication with applicants. % of Time 10 Duty/Responsibility General counseling to students and their families concerning the financial aid process, financial aid awards, and the status of individual applications for financial aid as well as providing general financial aid awareness through participation in workshops as needed. Position is also expected to work with the Director of Financial Aid to assist in the key, peak times. % of Time 15 Duty/Responsibility Assist families, students, campus offices and outside organizations with on site campus visits, which include but are not limited to campus tours, and meetings with faculty and staff. % of Time 15 Duty/Responsibility Counselor will assist with the Scholars of Distinction program, Discover Days, Open Houses, SAT prep program and other programs in maintaining student contact and assisting with the organization attendant with allied on campus programs. % of Time 10 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification A bachelor’s degree with general knowledge of higher education, marketing, and recruitment is required. A valid driver’s license is required. Required Skills Specific knowledge of college policies and procedures, college curriculum, admissions requirements, and financial aid procedures. Basic computer and travel skills, knowledge of the Banner database management system or the ability to learn such quickly. Great team player and attitude Ability to drive and travel extensively Required Experience Type of experience Needed Financial aid and admissions procedures Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) Type of experience Needed Large and small group presentations/public relations Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) Type of experience Needed Basic computer applications Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Concord University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a state Normal School to prepare teachers, Concord University (CU) is a public, career focused liberal arts institution located in rural southern West Virginia. Concord University (CU) offers talented individuals a wide array of fulfilling career opportunities from entry through academic or administrative professional levels. To maintain an outstanding talent pool, we employ individuals regionally, nationally, and internationally to attract top candidates. If you are looking for more than just a job, then I encourage you to browse our website and visit our job opportunities regularly. Learn more about Concord University and why it should be your first choice, not only for quality educational opportunities but also for exemplary employment. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply. This is a temporary, full-time position. Temporary positions are not eligible for Concord University employee benefits, except as may be required by applicable law. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/2954 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3372": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Concord University is a small liberal arts college located in scenic Athens, WV near Pipestem State Park. Our campus offers a close-knit academic community and a beautiful rural setting that fosters engaged teaching, scholarship, and collegial collaboration. Our rural location provides a welcoming community with opportunities for meaningful faculty-student interaction inside and outside the classroom. Application Process Applicants should submit Cover letter addressing teaching philosophy and research interests Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching (student evaluations or other documentation if available) Contact information for three professional references Applications received by May 15, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. At this time, the Department of Business will not provide H1B visa or employment sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Faculty Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Scheduled Hours Per Week Salary FLSA Status Exempt Job Summary Job Summary The Department of Business at Concord University invites applications for a tenure-track position in finance at the Assistant/Associate Professor level, effective August 2026. Concord University prides itself on a 150-year tradition of preparing students to enter the workforce or continue their education through graduate studies. We are seeking highly qualified individuals to join our faculty, who can apply their education and work experience to instruction that will enrich our students, further Concord’s commitment to programs of excellence, and reinforce CU’s mission to serve the region. This is a full-time, 9-month tenure-track faculty position that supports the departments’ two degree programs. The Department of Business offers an undergraduate degree program with concentrations in Accounting, Finance, Hospitality Management, Management, Marketing, and Sport Management. The Department also offers a 30-hour MBA program, as well as a Graduate Certificate in Human Resource Management. At this time, the Department of Business will not provide H1B visa or employment sponsorship. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Faculty members assume an active and collegial role in the planning and governance of the Department’s activities and expectations. Primary responsibilities include: Teaching a variety of undergraduate finance and related business courses (e.g. corporate finance, investments, personal finance, quantitative courses), along with a graduate class in finance with a 4/4 teaching load. Advising and mentoring students, participating in curriculum review and development, assessing and reporting of student learning, and reporting activities for program and university accreditation. Conducting scholarly research and being involved in the professional academic community.. Participating in service activities, which include serving on university and departmental committees, as well as service to the broader University community. % of Time 100% Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Doctorate Required Licenses/Certification Ph.D. in finance or related area or a DBA with a finance emphasis preferably from a regionally accredited institution. Individuals with a solid research background who are ABD at the final stage of completion of the dissertation may be considered. MBA business or other related master’s degree with substantial profession experience, may be considered for a non-tenure track position. Required Skills Demonstrate teaching competency and have a strong commitment to, and understanding of, the role of undergraduate and graduate business education. Demonstrate evidence of excellent oral and written English communication skills Provide evidence of interest in programmatic research and/or a prior record of publishing as we require and support faculty research productivity Understand the development of new course offerings in their disciple to support the department’s undergraduate and graduate programs. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Demonstrated teaching experience and competency Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Concord University is a small liberal arts college located in scenic Athens, WV near Pipestem State Park. Our campus offers a close-knit academic community and a beautiful rural setting that fosters engaged teaching, scholarship, and collegial collaboration. Our rural location provides a welcoming community with opportunities for meaningful faculty-student interaction inside and outside the classroom. Application Process Applicants should submit Cover letter addressing teaching philosophy and research interests Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching (student evaluations or other documentation if available) Contact information for three professional references Applications received by May 15, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. At this time, the Department of Business will not provide H1B visa or employment sponsorship. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/1321 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the United States? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3139": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant - Residence Life Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Graduate Assistant - Residence Life Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open to Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus monthly stipend provided. Can be renewed for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Hourly/Adjunct Position Title Graduate Assistant - Residence Life Working Title Graduate Assistant Resident Director Scheduled Hours Per Week Varies FLSA Status Job Summary Job Summary Reporting to the Director of Housing and Residence Life, the Graduate Assistant Resident Director is responsible for assisting with the management of one or more residence halls on the Concord University Campus. This is a live-in position that includes an on-campus apartment including utilities. In addition, on a rotating basis, the Graduate Resident Director and on-duty Public Safety Officer are the University’s point persons for emergency response on weekends and weeknights. The applicant must have at least two semesters of experience in Residence Life and be enrolled in a graduate program at Concord University (minimum 6 credit hours per semester). The Graduate Resident Director position requires a commitment to providing residential students with a safe living environment that fosters a strong sense of community, academic success, personal responsibility, and inclusiveness Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Day to Day physical and administrative operations of Residence Hall (including, but not limited to): Perform administrative duties including, but not limited to, room inspections, managing check-in and check-out, completing occupancy reports, completing incident reports, reporting and following up with work orders, stocking residence hall offices with all necessary paperwork and supplies, accompanying outside contractors, responding to lock outs, monthly safety reports, updating housing literature, and maintaining in-hall office hours. Perform night duty rounds approximately once a week and weekend duty rounds approximately once a month. Select, train, directly supervise, and evaluate all paraprofessional Resident Assistant and Desk Assistant staff employed in area(s) of supervision. Participate in development and implementation of programming activities, both on and off campus. Ensure that residents are aware of and adhering to the Residence Hall Policies and Procedures. Work with Facilities and Maintenance to ensure the physical needs of the Residence Halls are maintained. Maintain a close relationship with the Office of Public Safety. Various forms of involvement in the University judicial system. Respond to emergencies in the residence halls, defuse residential conflicts and crises, and provide mediation. Instruct staff and residents on fire safety, general evacuation procedures, and emergency protocols. Understanding and compliant with confidentiality, FERPA , and sensitive information. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Housing and Residence Life. % of Time 100 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification Driver’s License Required Skills Interpersonal and written/oral communications skills Technology skills (e.g., Microsoft Office – Excel, Word, PowerPoint, etc) Work independently Organizational skills and time management Understanding and compliant with confidentiality, FERPA and sensitive information Required Experience Type of experience Needed Residence Life / Student Affairs Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 1 year Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information This position is open to Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus monthly stipend provided. Can be renewed for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/1921 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3412": {
      "title": "Trade Specialist  II (HVAC)",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Trade Specialist  II (HVAC) Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Trade Specialist  II (HVAC) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Concord University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a state Normal School to prepare teachers, Concord University (CU) is a public, career focused liberal arts institution located in rural southern West Virginia. Concord University (CU) offers talented individuals a wide array of fulfilling career opportunities from entry through academic or administrative professional levels. To maintain an outstanding talent pool, we employ individuals regionally, nationally, and internationally to attract top candidates. If you are looking for more than just a job, then I encourage you to browse our website and visit our job opportunities regularly. Learn more about Concord University and why it should be your first choice, not only for quality educational opportunities but also for exemplary employment. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply. We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Concord University offers outstanding benefit packages including: Work week of 37.5 hrs. Holidays – Employees receive 13-14 Paid Holidays Annually Annual and Sick Leave –Staff earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. Health Insurance – Concord University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency (PEIA). Tuition and Fee Waivers- Professional development and education opportunities including tuition waiver program for employees, spouse, and eligible dependents. Retirement Plans – TIAA’s automatic retirement plan is a 401(a) plan into which six (6) percent of the employee’s total salary is automatically withheld pre-tax and deposited into the employee’s TIAA retirement account. The university matches the employees 6% contribution Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Mountaineer Flexible Benefits. This is an IRS approved, tax free account that saves money on eligible health, medical, dental, and dependent care expenses. Annual Increment Pay. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Staff Position Title Trade Specialist  II (HVAC) Working Title Trade Specialist II (HVAC) Scheduled Hours Per Week 37.5 FLSA Status Non-Exempt Job Summary Job Summary Concord University is seeking a skilled Trade Specialist II ( HVAC ) to support the safe, reliable, and efficient operation of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration systems across campus. This position is responsible for the installation, repair, replacement, inspection, and preventative maintenance of HVAC and refrigeration equipment throughout university facilities, including residence halls, academic and administrative buildings, faculty housing, and the President’s residence. The Trade Specialist II will also maintain and repair ice-making machines, commercial refrigeration systems, and food preparation equipment within the university’s dining facilities. The position plays an important role in maintaining comfortable, functional, and safe environments for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position requires a strong working knowledge of HVAC and refrigeration systems, the ability to troubleshoot and resolve equipment issues, and a commitment to quality workmanship, safety, and responsive customer service. The successful candidate will work independently and as part of the Facilities team to address routine maintenance needs, emergency repairs, and preventative maintenance throughout campus. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility The ability to read schematics and troubleshoot circuits at the unit. Repair and maintain electrical H.V.A.C. controls and refrigeration circuits. Maintain steam absorption equipment and provide yearly rebuilding, as well as daily and weekly inspections. Repair and replace refrigeration equipment in the kitchen, walk-in coolers, walk-in freezers, ice machines, reach-in coolers and freezers, and all food preparation equipment. Recover refrigerants and remove old equipment and replace. Operate recovery machines properly. Know and execute E.P.A. rules and regulations in the handling of refrigerants. Replace and repair window air conditioner units. Keep logs and records of recovered refrigerants and refrigerant usage. Troubleshoot and repair complex pneumatic and electronic controls such as transducers, receiver controllers, thermostats P.E. switches, etc. Replace split-system air conditioning units, condensing units, air handlers and heat pumps. Maintain and operate feed water pumps, chemicals, and feed water levels in boilers. Repair and maintain heating and cooling systems in the President’s House, Witherspoon faculty housing, Mill Street Apartments, and all other buildings on campus. Repair and maintain steam boilers as well as hot water boilers. % of Time 45% Duty/Responsibility Perform repairs of electrical, plumbing, heating and carpentry as the situation requires. Use various construction methods and practices as required to perform essential tasks related to maintenance and repair of buildings and equipment. % of Time 20% Duty/Responsibility Operate utilities Energy Management System to monitor and maintain building environments on campus and back up capacity. Maintenance and upkeep of campus generators, kitchen dish belt and bread proofers. % of Time 10% Duty/Responsibility Maintain air handlers, exhaust systems, (Balance air hoods, exhaust fans, and dampers) replacing filters, cleaning and repair coils, changing belts etc., as required. Install and maintain building control systems using both pneumatic and electrical equipment. Install and maintain cooling towers, consisting of water treatment, cleaning, repairing and inspection for proper operation. Interpret blueprints and specifications for HC/AC/R equipment to ensure proper installation and operation. Prepare requisition for parts, supplies, etc., from supply rooms and tool crib to ensure proper installation. Operate heavy equipment as assigned. Install and maintain heating exchangers, hot and chilled water treatments. Welding as assigned by supervisor. Other duties as assigned. % of Time 25% Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Business/Technical/Vocational School Required Licenses/Certification Must hold required certification in H.V.A.C. (Required by state law) and renewed annually. Universal Refrigeration certification – required by federal law. OSHA 10 hour certification – institutional requirement. 410A Licensure – Institutional requirement. EPA Section 608 certification Certificate Training required under 609 for proper use of motor vehicle A.C. – institutional requirement. Required Skills Knowledge and skilled in the areas of steam technology, refrigeration pneumatics, and energy management technology. All phases of heating, ventilation, air conditioning and refrigeration (HV/AC/R. Knowledge of materials such as asbestos, bromide, CFC’s, and water treatment chemicals for HV/AC/R equipment. Knowledge of materials, methods, tools, equipment installation and controls (electrical and pneumatic). Ability to safely use hand tools, power tools, testing equipment, ladders, scaffolds, and other equipment required for the position. Ability to work effectively with maintenance and Facilities personnel and respond to routine and emergency maintenance needs. Ability to work in extreme temperatures, elevated noise levels, poor lighting, limited ventilation, confined spaces, and other challenging work environments. Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position, including walking, stooping, crouching, climbing, reaching, and working from ladders and scaffolds. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Experience in HV/AC/R, electrical, sheet metal Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Type of experience Needed Instrumentation controls and computer Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Type of experience Needed Operation control in DDC, electrical and pneumatice Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Type of experience Needed Refrigeration and kitchen equipment Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Concord University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a state Normal School to prepare teachers, Concord University (CU) is a public, career focused liberal arts institution located in rural southern West Virginia. Concord University (CU) offers talented individuals a wide array of fulfilling career opportunities from entry through academic or administrative professional levels. To maintain an outstanding talent pool, we employ individuals regionally, nationally, and internationally to attract top candidates. If you are looking for more than just a job, then I encourage you to browse our website and visit our job opportunities regularly. Learn more about Concord University and why it should be your first choice, not only for quality educational opportunities but also for exemplary employment. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply. We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Concord University offers outstanding benefit packages including: Work week of 37.5 hrs. Holidays – Employees receive 13-14 Paid Holidays Annually Annual and Sick Leave –Staff earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. Health Insurance – Concord University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). Tuition and Fee Waivers- Professional development and education opportunities including tuition waiver program for employees, spouse, and eligible dependents. Retirement Plans – TIAA’s automatic retirement plan is a 401(a) plan into which six (6) percent of the employee’s total salary is automatically withheld pre-tax and deposited into the employee’s TIAA retirement account. The university matches the employees 6% contribution Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Mountaineer Flexible Benefits. This is an IRS approved, tax free account that saves money on eligible health, medical, dental, and dependent care expenses. Annual Increment Pay. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/1845 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
