    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3301": {
      "title": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Nursing Faculty Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Adjunct Nursing Faculty Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Concord University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a state Normal School to prepare teachers, Concord University (CU) is a public, career focused institution located in rural southern West Virginia. Concord University (CU) offers talented individuals a wide array of fulfilling career opportunities from entry-level to academic and administrative professional roles. To maintain an outstanding talent pool, we employ individuals regionally, nationally, and internationally to attract top candidates. If you are looking for more than just a job, then I encourage you to browse our website and regularly check our job opportunities. Learn more about Concord University and why it should be your first choice, not only for quality educational opportunities but also for exemplary employment. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Faculty Position Title Adjunct Nursing Faculty Working Title Adjunct Nursing Faculty Scheduled Hours Per Week PRN - As needed per semester FLSA Status Job Summary Job Summary The Department of Nursing is seeking applicants for adjunct appointments to serve as clinical and academic adjuncts in our Bachelor of Science in Nursing program. This is on a semester-to-semester basis as needed. Successful candidates are expected to have a willingness and desire to engage in student success and development in both the clinical and academic settings, as required, with an emphasis placed on the clinical setting. Successful candidates should also maintain the mission of the Nursing Education Program, Department of Nursing, and Concord University while adhering to all West Virginia RN Board, Title 19 Series 1, rules/regulations, as well as adhere to the Nurse Practice Act of West Virginia. Assignments are based on course availability and expertise. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Prepares and delivers instruction, setting high and challenging academic standards, to students in assigned modalities (including classroom, clinical, hybrid, online, etc.) Prepares instructional materials such as lectures, presentations, lab sessions, clinical and cooperative arrangements Uses various learning assessments to evaluate student mastery of course and program outcomes Provides feedback on student’s progress, in a timely manner, to facilitate academic success Prepares and submits required documentation, including course syllabi, student attendance, final course grades, and other information as requested or required by the university and faculty member mentor Maintains professional development/growth according to personal needs and requirements for certification and licensure. Performs other job-related duties and projects as assigned in support of the University’s mission, core values and goals. % of Time 100% Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification For clinical assignment: Bachelor’s degree with 3+ years of experience in the clinical setting. For academic assignment: Master’s degree with experience in nursing education in the classroom or clinical setting. Required Skills MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR CLINICAL ASSIGNMENT Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing 3+ years of experience in the clinical setting Current licensure as a Registered Nurse with an active Nurse Licensure Compact ( NLC ) license or be willing to obtain a compact state registered nurse license. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR ACADEMIC ASSIGNMENT Master’s Degree in Nursing or advanced nurse practitioner Current licensure as a Registered Nurse with an active Nurse Licensure Compact ( NLC ) license or be willing to obtain a compact state registered nurse license. 3+ years of clinical practice and/or classroom experience PREFERED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Nursing Prior classroom experience Prior clinical experience and interdisciplinary collaboration The ideal candidate will be dually experienced as both an academic and clinical provider. Three or more years of teaching experience preferred. Strong collegial and collaborative skills Experience teaching face-to-face and online courses Experience as a preceptor in a nationally accredited program Working knowledge of national accreditation practices and policies Current licensure as a Registered Nurse with an active Nurse Licensure Compact ( NLC ) license or be willing to obtain a compact state registered nurse license. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Clinical practice and classroom experience Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 3 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Concord University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a state Normal School to prepare teachers, Concord University (CU) is a public, career focused institution located in rural southern West Virginia. Concord University (CU) offers talented individuals a wide array of fulfilling career opportunities from entry-level to academic and administrative professional roles. To maintain an outstanding talent pool, we employ individuals regionally, nationally, and internationally to attract top candidates. If you are looking for more than just a job, then I encourage you to browse our website and regularly check our job opportunities. Learn more about Concord University and why it should be your first choice, not only for quality educational opportunities but also for exemplary employment. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3300 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
