    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3392": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for XC and Track",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant for XC and Track Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Graduate Assistant for XC and Track Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. May be renewable for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Graduate Assistant Position Title Graduate Assistant for XC and Track Working Title Assistant XC and Track Coach Scheduled Hours Per Week 20 FLSA Status Job Summary Job Summary The Graduate Assistant for Cross Country & Track will play a vital role in supporting the coaching staff in all aspects of the cross country and track & field programs. This is a 10-month position designed for a graduate student pursuing a degree at Concord university. The GA will assist in training, recruiting, event planning, administrative tasks, and athlete development for both men’s and women’s teams. This role offers a unique opportunity to gain practical coaching experience while working with athletes in a dynamic and competitive collegiate athletic environment. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Assist in planning, organizing, and implementing daily practice sessions for cross country and track & field athletes. Provide guidance and support during training sessions, including warm-ups, drills, and conditioning. Attend and assist with team practices, workouts, and competitions (including travel, if needed). Monitor athletes’ physical and academic progress and communicate with the coaching staff to ensure overall success. Assist with recruiting efforts, including identifying and evaluating potential student-athletes. Attend recruiting events and help with campus visits for prospective athletes. Assist with meet preparation and coordination, including entries, travel arrangements, and logistics. Assist with organizing team meetings, events, and communication with athletes. Aid in the planning and execution of team camps, fundraising events, and community outreach programs. Other Duties as assigned by the Head Men’s and Women’s XC and Track Coach, and Athletic Directors % of Time 100 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification Driver License USATF Officials Certification (Preferred) Required Skills Working knowledge of and familiarity with NCAA rules and regulations. Excellent written and verbal communication, presentation, interpersonal, and analytical skills. Demonstrated interpersonal and organizational skills. Required Experience Type of experience Needed College experience in XC or Track coaching or playing Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. May be renewable for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3253 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3363": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. About the Department The Department of Business at Concord University is a community of faculty, scholars, and practitioners committed to developing the next generation of business professionals. Our faculty bring both academic expertise and real-world experience to the classroom, and we take pride in the close faculty-student relationships that define a Concord education. About Concord University Concord University is a small public, comprehensive institution with an enrollment of approximately 1,800 students. Located in Athens, West Virginia near Pipestem State Park, the University offers a close-knit academic community and a beautiful rural setting that fosters engaged teaching, scholarship, and collegial collaboration. Athens is within driving distance of metropolitan areas in West Virginia, Virginia, North Carolina, and Washington, D.C. Concord has a strong commitment to the principle of diversity and seeks a broad representation of candidates, including women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. Compensation- Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Visa Sponsorship- At this time, the Department of Business will not provide H1B visa or employment sponsorship. Application Process Applicants should submit: Cover letter specific to the position, interest in working at Concord University, and relocating to southern West Virginia Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching (student evaluations or other documentation if available) Unofficial transcripts Contact information for three professional references Applications received by May 15th will receive full consideration . Review will continue until the position is filled. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University's online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Faculty Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Scheduled Hours Per Week Salary FLSA Status Exempt Job Summary Job Summary The Department of Business at Concord University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Business at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, effective August 2026. Concord University prides itself on a 150-year tradition of preparing students to enter the workforce or continue their education through graduate studies. We are seeking highly qualified individuals to join our faculty who can apply their education and professional experience to instruction that will enrich our students, further Concord’s commitment to programs of excellence, and reinforce CU’s mission to serve the region. This is a full-time, 9-month tenure-track faculty position that supports the department’s degree programs. The Department of Business offers an undergraduate degree program with concentrations in Accounting, Finance, Hospitality Management, Management, Marketing, and Sport Management. The Department also offers a 30-hour MBA program, as well as a Graduate Certificate in Human Resource Management. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Faculty members assume an active and collegial role in the planning and governance of the Department’s activities and expectations. Primary responsibilities include: Teaching a variety of undergraduate and graduate business courses with a 4/4 teaching load, with primary responsibility for courses in management and operations, including Business Statistics and Business Analytics. Participating in continuous improvement activities to strive to improve effectiveness of teaching and maintain currency of the academic discipline. Advising and mentoring students, participating in curriculum review and development, and assessing and reporting student learning outcomes and accreditation-related activities. Conducting scholarly research and engaging with the professional academic community. Participating in service activities, including serving on university and departmental committees, attending faculty and departmental meetings, and contributing to the broader University community. % of Time 100 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Master's Required Licenses/Certification A Ph.D. or DBA in a business-related field from a regionally accredited institution is required, with a preference for candidates with a background in Management, Operations Management, Supply Chain, or a closely related discipline. Candidates with a quantitative background or research focus are especially encouraged to apply. A doctorate is required for tenure consideration. Candidates holding an MBA or master’s degree in a related field, combined with substantial professional experience, may be considered for a non-tenure track appointment. Required Skills Demonstrated teaching competency and a strong commitment to undergraduate and graduate business education is preferred, but candidates with relevant professional experience will be reviewed. Proficiency or demonstrated experience with analytics tools such as Excel, R, Python, Tableau, or similar software is a plus. Excellent oral and written English communication skills. Evidence of interest in programmatic research and/or a prior record of publishing, as we require and support faculty research productivity. Understanding of course development to support evolving undergraduate and graduate program needs. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Teaching experience preferred. Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Type of experience Needed Professional or industry experience in management, operations, or a related field is a plus. Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information About the Department The Department of Business at Concord University is a community of faculty, scholars, and practitioners committed to developing the next generation of business professionals. Our faculty bring both academic expertise and real-world experience to the classroom, and we take pride in the close faculty-student relationships that define a Concord education. About Concord University Concord University is a small public, comprehensive institution with an enrollment of approximately 1,800 students. Located in Athens, West Virginia near Pipestem State Park, the University offers a close-knit academic community and a beautiful rural setting that fosters engaged teaching, scholarship, and collegial collaboration. Athens is within driving distance of metropolitan areas in West Virginia, Virginia, North Carolina, and Washington, D.C. Concord has a strong commitment to the principle of diversity and seeks a broad representation of candidates, including women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. Compensation- Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Visa Sponsorship- At this time, the Department of Business will not provide H1B visa or employment sponsorship. Application Process Applicants should submit: Cover letter specific to the position, interest in working at Concord University, and relocating to southern West Virginia Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching (student evaluations or other documentation if available) Unofficial transcripts Contact information for three professional references Applications received by May 15th will receive full consideration . Review will continue until the position is filled. Applications will only be accepted through Concord University’s online application site at https://jobs.concord.edu/. Concord University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/2837 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Optional Documents Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3083": {
      "title": "Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Women&#39;s Basketball Graduate Assistant Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. May be renewable for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Graduate Assistant Position Title Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant Working Title Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant Scheduled Hours Per Week 20 FLSA Status Non-Exempt Job Summary Job Summary The Women’s Basketball Graduate Assistant position shall be responsible for assisting with the daily operations of the women’s basketball program. The GA will assist with recruiting, game planning, and all aspects of the Division II Basketball program in compliance with all NCAA , MEC Conference and institutional rules and regulations. This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Assist with practice planning and coaching during team practices Assist with the monitoring of weight room and strength training programs Assist with the organization and coordination of on-campus recruitment of prospective student-athletes and coordination of all recruitment mailings and correspondence Assist program staff and assistant coaches with team travel needs Coordinate with equipment and coaching staffs to ensure the organization of practice and travel gear Other duties as assigned by the Head Women’s Coach % of Time 100 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification Job Requirements: -Applicants must have earned a bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. -Applicants will be required to be accepted and enroll in a Graduate level program at Concord University. -Candidates will have a working knowledge of the game of basketball, playing experience preferred but not required. -Applicants must have strong communication, interpersonal and organizational skills. -Candidate will abide by all University and NCAA Rules and Regulations and laws of the state of West Virginia. Required Skills Working knowledge of and familiarity with NCAA rules and regulations. Excellent written and verbal communication, presentation, interpersonal, and analytical skills. Demonstrated interpersonal and organizational skills. Required Experience Type of experience Needed One year experience in a college basketball setting (years as a player can be counted). Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) Over 1 Year, up to 2 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. May be renewable for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3082 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
