    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3373": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Athletics",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant Athletics Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Graduate Assistant Athletics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. May be renewable for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Applicants should submit: Resume Cover letter indicating which GA position(s) they wish to be considered for Contact information for three professional references Applicants with sport‑specific questions are encouraged to contact the Athletic Director or the head coach of the respective program for additional information about individual roles. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Graduate Assistant Position Title Graduate Assistant Athletics Working Title Graduate Assistant Athletics Scheduled Hours Per Week 20 FLSA Status Non-Exempt Job Summary Job Summary Concord University is seeking qualified applicants for multiple Graduate Assistant (GA) positions within the Department of Athletics for the 2026–2027 academic year . These positions offer hands‑on professional experience in collegiate athletics while supporting the operational, coaching, and administrative needs of our NCAA Division II programs. Available Graduate Assistant Positions Women’s Soccer – Graduate Assistant Coach Men’s Soccer – Graduate Assistant Coach Track & Field – Graduate Assistant Coach Athletic Training – Graduate Assistant Softball – Graduate Assistant Coach Women’s Basketball – Graduate Assistant Coach Men’s Basketball – Graduate Assistant Coach The GA will assist with recruiting, game planning and all aspects of the Division II program in compliance with all NCAA , MEC Conference and institutional rules and regulations. This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Responsibilities will vary by sport or assignment but may include: Assisting with practice planning, instruction, and skill development Supporting game‑day operations, travel logistics, and equipment management Recruiting prospective student‑athletes in compliance with NCAA and Mountain East Conference regulations Assisting with strength and conditioning programming Supporting academic monitoring and student‑athlete development initiatives Completing administrative duties assigned by the head coach or supervising athletic staff Athletic Training GA: Assisting with injury prevention, evaluation, rehabilitation, and event coverage under the supervision of certified athletic trainers % of Time 100 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Bachelor's Required Licenses/Certification Driver’s license. Admission to a Concord University graduate program (required for employment) Athletic Training GA: must meet CAATE and West Virginia licensure eligibility requirements Required Skills Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required Collegiate playing or coaching experience Experience working in a team‑oriented environment Familiarity with NCAA Division II rules and regulations Required Experience Type of experience Needed Playing and / or Coaching Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 2 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information This position is open to Concord Graduate Students only. Full tuition waiver plus competitive stipend provided. May be renewable for additional academic terms based on satisfactory performance of duties and student enrollment as a CU graduate student. Applicants should submit: Resume Cover letter indicating which GA position(s) they wish to be considered for Contact information for three professional references Applicants with sport‑specific questions are encouraged to contact the Athletic Director or the head coach of the respective program for additional information about individual roles. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/1676 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3279": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Political Science",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty – Political Science Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Adjunct Faculty – Political Science Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Requirements for Completed Application. - Letter of application - CV - Unofficial copy of transcripts (The selected candidate will be required to submit official copies of transcripts before time of appointment - Three references and their contact information (including a current address, phone number and e-mail address) Interested individuals should upload a cover letter, resume/curriculum vita, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial transcripts, and the names and contact information for at least three references. These materials will be kept on file and the department chair will contact potential adjuncts on as needed basis to teach fall, spring, or summer courses. Applications for part-time faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed by the department chair when openings become available. Postings close yearly on January 31; to maintain your application within the system, you will need to re-apply each year. All application materials should be submitted through the HR web portal. Concord University is a public, liberal-arts institution with an enrollment of approximately 2000 students. The University is located in a scenic, small-town setting in the mountains of southern West Virginia with access to year-round outdoor recreation activities. The Department values and actively supports innovative teaching and participation in undergraduate research and seeks candidates with similar ideals. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Hourly/Adjunct Position Title Adjunct Faculty – Political Science Working Title Adjunct Faculty – Political Science Scheduled Hours Per Week FLSA Status Exempt Job Summary Job Summary The Department of Social Sciences is seeking applications for in-person adjunct faculty in Political Science. The adjunct instructor is responsible for the planning, presentation, and evaluation of classroom instruction and related activities. Qualified adjuncts must have a Master’s degree in Political Science, Public Administration, or a related field. Prior teaching experience in higher education preferred. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility Prepares and delivers in-person instruction on topics in American Federal Government, State and Local Government, and other courses on the University’s main campus in Athens, WV. Compiles, administers, evaluates, and grades students’ assignments, tests, and papers fairly and consistently and keeps students informed about their progress through the prompt grading of papers and other work. Contributes to General Education and Program Assessment through the collection and reporting of course data. Develops curricula and instructional material such as syllabi, homework assignments, and handouts. Maintains office hours for students seeking academic advice, assist in student recruitment and retention, and assists students with course-related problems outside of the classroom. Maintains accurate student attendance records, grades, and other required records in compliance with federal FERPA regulations. May perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair or Dean. % of Time 100 Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Master's Required Licenses/Certification Master’s degree in Political Science, Public Administration, or a related field. Required Skills Skill in selecting and using training/instructional methods and procedures appropriate for the situation when learning or teaching new things. Knowledge and understanding of a college academic environment. Knowledge of current teaching and learning strategies to facilitate student-centered learning; experience interacting successfully with academically and culturally diverse student populations. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Teaching experience preferred. Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 1 year Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Requirements for Completed Application. - Letter of application - CV - Unofficial copy of transcripts (The selected candidate will be required to submit official copies of transcripts before time of appointment - Three references and their contact information (including a current address, phone number and e-mail address) Interested individuals should upload a cover letter, resume/curriculum vita, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial transcripts, and the names and contact information for at least three references. These materials will be kept on file and the department chair will contact potential adjuncts on as needed basis to teach fall, spring, or summer courses. Applications for part-time faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed by the department chair when openings become available. Postings close yearly on January 31; to maintain your application within the system, you will need to re-apply each year. All application materials should be submitted through the HR web portal. Concord University is a public, liberal-arts institution with an enrollment of approximately 2000 students. The University is located in a scenic, small-town setting in the mountains of southern West Virginia with access to year-round outdoor recreation activities. The Department values and actively supports innovative teaching and participation in undergraduate research and seeks candidates with similar ideals. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3001 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
  },
